From 619af7280982895d74703281cfc07529864f27fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: litlfred <leitnerc@who.int>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:30:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] QR Code Generation: live examples of each step and of
 verification

Each step of the page gets a live example that runs in the reader's
browser, using the WebAssembly build of litlfred/smart-trust-tools'
hcert library (input/images/hcert-demo/, built by its bundle-demo.sh
with the commit and hashes recorded in SOURCE.md):

- a key pair the browser generates (ES256 or PS256, WebCrypto,
  non-extractable) and a self-signed TEST ONLY DSC for it;
- Steps 1 to 8, which share one certificate, so an edit to the payload
  re-runs every later step;
- verification, with each step of section 11 marked, buttons that
  change one character or one signature byte, and a choice of trusting
  the page's DSC, a DSC the reader pastes, or nothing;
- the two certificates of section 12.6 (DEV participant XXR), decoded
  live; pasting their DSC from the GDHCN DEV trust list verifies them
  in the browser, and without it verification stops at the trust
  lookup, as section 12.6 says it should.

Nothing made on the page verifies anywhere else: its DSC is self-signed
by test participant XX and is on no trust list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018yS1p2XbAXk8awZpAgSNQ2
